    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0100261 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0100261">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0011842"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An abnormality of the structure or form of the tendons, also often called sinews.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154"/>
        <dcterms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-07-20T01:20:19Z</dcterms:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C4021026</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Abnormal shape of tendon</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="fr">Abnormal shape of tendon|Abnormality of the sinew</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Abnormality of the sinew</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0100261</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>A tendon (or sinew) is a tough band of fibrous connective tissue that usually connects muscle to bone and is capable of withstanding tension. Tendons are similar to ligaments and fascia as they are all made of collagen except that ligaments join one bone to another bone, and fascia connect muscles to other muscles. Tendons and muscles work together and can only exert a pulling force.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Abnormal tendon morphology</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="es">Morfología del tendón anormal</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">Morphologie anormale des tendons</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0100261"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
